# The ticket briefs are hashed over their RAW BYTES, with no normalisation of any
# kind (see `ticketDigest` in ../src/hash.ts). A checkout that converted line
# endings would change all six digests at once, silently, on a machine that never
# edited a ticket — and `verifyFrozen()` would correctly but uselessly refuse to
# run the campaign.
#
# `-text` disables git's end-of-line conversion entirely for this directory:
# whatever bytes were committed are the bytes on disk, on every platform. This
# covers the repo-checkout failure path. The editor failure path is covered
# separately by src/tickets.ts, which refuses to load a brief containing a CR or
# a byte-order mark.
* -text
